  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 233 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nHot and humid conditions are forecast to continue into early next \nweek. High temperatures on Monday will be very similar to those on \nSunday, but some relief is possible by Tuesday as the late-weekend \nshortwave trough dives southeastward into the Great Lakes and Ohio \nValley. While the associated cold front is not particularly strong, \nit will help temper the heat and humidity. Temperatures on Tuesday \nwill still reach the upper 80s to lower 90s, but surface dewpoints \nare expected to drop by 10 to 15 degrees, yielding noticeably lower \nrelative humidity values. Unfortunately, the overarching synoptic \npattern will not break down, and warm temperatures will persist \nthrough the remainder of the forecast period. However, some \ntemporary relief may occur via potential MCS activity along the ring \nof fire in northwesterly flow around the upper ridge centered over \nthe Desert Southwest.\n\nDangerous heat and humidity will linger through Monday before a weak \ncold front provides slight relief on Tuesday. While high \ntemperatures Tuesday will remain in the upper 80s and lower 90s, \nnoticeably lower dewpoints will lower relative humidity values. The \nhot pattern will persist through the rest of the week, with \nadditional rain and temperature breaks tied to potential night-to-\nmorning MCS activity traveling along the ridge periphery.",
